WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.940
An X-Files star Hulking out?

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.790
Blade becoming the Black Panther?

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.630
These may seem like deep pulls from the far
recesses of the multiverse, but they came

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.020
closer to our reality than you might imagine.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.060
Keep watching for more actors who were almost
Avengers.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.350
The MCU was practically built on Robert Downey
Jr.'s shoulders, but he wasn't always a shoe-in

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.560
for Iron Man.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.119
After the actor's history of drug and alcohol
abuse landed him in prison, studios considered

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:33.980
him to be "box office poison" and a risky
investment for future movies.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.200
You know who isn't risky business?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.200
Tom Cruise.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.300
In fact, Cruise has been one of the most bankable
stars in Hollywood for decades.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.790
While he claims he never came close to playing
Iron Man, Marvel Chief Kevin Feige said in

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:52.190
2004 that the studio had been talking to the
actor since the late '90s — but no deal

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.740
was ever made.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:58.090
Many assumed it all came down to money, and,
while the then-fledgling Marvel Studios couldn't

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.590
afford Cruise, they could afford Robert Downey
Jr.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:06.420
It was a risky move at the time, but Downey's
casting has worked out pretty well for both

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.420
sides.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.530
The actor's rapscallion wit and heroic heart
of gold have not just defined the character,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.490
but the MCU as a whole.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.479
Basically: no RDJ, no MCU.

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:21.180
And Tom Cruise concurs, too, having once said
of Downey's performance:

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.939
"I can't imagine anyone else in that role,
and I think it's perfect for him."

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:30.060
Honestly, you'd struggle to find anyone who
disagrees.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.009
Tom Cruise may have been the most bankable
movie star to circle the role of Tony Stark,

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:36.950
but he wasn't the only one.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.820
One actor who came especially close to donning
the red and gold was Sam Rockwell, who was

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:46.810
previously best known for movies such as Lawn
Dogs and The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:50.780
"If there's anything more important than my
ego on this ship, I want it caught and shot

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.780
right now."

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.969
In fact, Iron Man director and MCU producer
Jon Favreau personally asked Rockwell to audition

00:01:56.969 --> 00:01:57.969
for the role.

00:01:57.969 --> 00:02:02.689
Alas, it wasn't to be, though it's not like
Rockwell hasn't enjoyed a pretty remarkable

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:08.710
career since 2008, most notably winning an
Academy Award for his turn in Three Billboards

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.100
Outside Ebbing, Missouri.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.871
He even got his chance to play in the MCU
sandbox, having gyrated his way into the role

00:02:14.871 --> 00:02:19.640
of Justin Hammer in Iron Man 2 — and with
the character rumored to appear in the upcoming

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.959
Armor Wars series, it seems like Rockwell
may not be done with the Marvel Universe just yet.

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:31.430
Before Chadwick Boseman donned the now-iconic
mask of Black Panther, Wesley Snipes set his

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.900
sights on playing Wakanda's warrior king.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.099
In the mid-1990s, Snipes was enjoying some
serious box office clout after a string of

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:44.069
hits, and wanted to bring Black Panther to
the big screen, believing it could be a blockbuster

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:45.930
and cultural milestone.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.430
Recently, Snipes told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:53.319
"Black Panther is an iconic character who
much of the world was unfamiliar with and

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:56.760
the communities that I grew up in would love."

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.909
Snipes was right, too — he was just a quarter
of a century too early.

00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:06.220
In the mid-1990s, Batman was the only superhero
making movies, CGI wasn't ready to realize

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.299
Wakanda, and Marvel even declared bankruptcy
in 1996.

00:03:10.299 --> 00:03:14.569
To make matters more difficult, when studios
heard the name "Black Panther," they thought

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:18.750
of 1960s social revolutionaries rather than
superheroes.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.780
Snipes used the experience to launch the highly
successful Blade franchise, while Black Panther

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:29.340
itself became the highest-grossing domestic
superhero release nearly three decades later.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.430
And Snipes couldn't be happier.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.430
He said:

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:38.500
"Even though I am not a part of this particular
project, I support it 1,000 percent, and I

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:44.090
am absolutely convinced that it will be a
catalyst for change and open other doors and

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.170
other opportunities."

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:50.620
Over the years, the role of Bruce Banner has
seemed like a never-ending game of musical

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.620
chairs.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.519
After Eric Bana and before Edward Norton,
the front runner to take the role was Fox

00:03:56.519 --> 00:03:58.900
Mulder himself, David Duchovny.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.790
Bana, who starred in Ang Lee's Hulk in 2003,
dropped out of the franchise when he discovered

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.440
the sequel was set to be straight-to-DVD.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:10.900
Duchovny's frontrunner status was revealed
by Marvel's then-vice chairman Peter Cuneo

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.180
[CUE-nee-oh] back in 2006.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:17.419
How close Duchovny came to getting the part
is unclear, however; All we know is that he

00:04:17.419 --> 00:04:22.419
obviously didn't get the role, and that the
straight-to-DVD sequel to Lee's film was scrapped

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:23.419
altogether.

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:28.190
Instead, Edward Norton got the part in The
Incredible Hulk, which basically rebooted

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:32.979
the franchise into the new continuity of the
MCU after the successful debut of Iron Man

00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:34.199
a year earlier.

00:04:34.199 --> 00:04:39.500
Norton famously got himself fired from the
franchise soon after, leaving Marvel on pretty

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.669
bad terms.

00:04:40.669 --> 00:04:45.479
He was subsequently replaced by Mark Ruffalo,
who has played the part to perfection ever

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:46.479
since.

00:04:46.479 --> 00:04:47.789
"Hulk out!"

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:48.789
"Bruce."

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:49.789
"Dab!"

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.789
"Bruce."

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:53.169
"Listen to your mom!

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:54.169
She knows better."

00:04:55.169 --> 00:04:58.380
Marvel has evidently wanted to work with Emily
Blunt for some time now.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:03.190
The British-born thespian has apparently been
offered not one, but two critical roles in

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:08.220
the MCU — Peggy Carter in Captain America:
The First Avenger and Black Widow in Iron

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.220
Man 2.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:13.280
Of course, the former part went to Haley Atwell,
while Scarlett Johansson has been a key player

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.490
in the Avengers movies and beyond ever since
her MCU debut.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:22.180
There are many reasons Blunt didn't take the
Widow role, and she herself has claimed it

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.220
was all down to scheduling conflicts.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.900
She refuses to discuss parts she didn't accept
in detail, however, saying it's unfair to

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.759
the actors who ended up playing them.

00:05:30.759 --> 00:05:35.580
Still, there are plenty of female roles still
to come in the ever-expanding Marvel Universe,

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:40.270
so fingers crossed Blunt will turn up sometime
in the not-so-distant future.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.620
Emily Blunt wasn't the only member of her
household to almost appear in the MCU.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.790
Her husband, John Krasinski, very nearly donned
the red, white and blue of the star-spangled

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.360
Avenger, Captain America.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:58.080
As his role as Jack Ryan has proven, he's
more than capable of playing a patriotic super-soldier

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.770
— but it wasn't Marvel who pulled the plug
on Krasinski playing the part.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.490
It was the actor himself.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:08.360
According to Krasinski, he got as far as a
costumed audition, during which he saw Chris

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.180
Hemsworth walk by in full Thor regalia.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:16.060
In that moment, Krasinski realized what he
was about to get himself into and had a change

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.060
of heart.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.099
"Chris Hemsworth walked by as Thor, and he's
like, 'hey mate,' and I'm like, 'I'm good.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:26.670
This is stupid.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.670
It's okay, I'm not Captain America.'"

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:31.970
Krasinski's decision may seem like madness
to many, but if you've ever watched a behind-the-scenes

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:37.610
video of actors wearing $100,000 Halloween
costumes and staring at ten-foot tennis balls

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:41.419
surrounded by green screens, you can probably
see his point.

00:06:41.419 --> 00:06:45.069
And hey, Chris Evans is nothing to be sniffed
at, either.

00:06:46.069 --> 00:06:48.020
How's this for a sibling rivalry?

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:52.660
Before Chris Hemsworth was cast as the god
of thunder in 2011's Thor, his younger brother

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.560
Liam was one of the frontrunners for the part.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.569
Early in his career, the tall and lanky Chris
Hemsworth had been having trouble finding

00:06:58.569 --> 00:07:02.990
parts that suited his frame, when he spotted
a call sheet for Thor that required an actor

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:06.210
of at least 6'3" and 200 lbs.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:09.960
Hemsworth auditioned for director Kenneth
Branagh and thought he nailed it... but he

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.510
didn't hear back for months.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:15.580
Meanwhile, his little brother Liam, still
back home in Australia, had sent in a taped

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.060
audition and was subsequently called back
several times.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:23.860
Liam was one of the final five, in fact, when
Chris' manager contacted the movie's casting

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:27.270
team, reminding them Liam had an older brother.

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:32.409
Chris got another audition and must have impressed
this time, as he was cast in the role soon after.

00:07:33.299 --> 00:07:38.320
As hard as it is to imagine anybody but Chris
Pratt playing Peter Quill, Guardians of the

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.550
Galaxy director James Gunn had a backup plan
for the part.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:42.550
He once told GQ:

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:47.970
"There was a good chance that, if I didn't
cast Chris, that I would've cast Glenn Howerton

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:49.099
in the role."

00:07:49.099 --> 00:07:54.730
Howerton most famously plays the morally reprehensible
Dennis on the long-running FX sitcom, It's

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:59.250
Always Sunny In Philadelphia, a character
who is about as far away from Star-Lord as

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.370
you can possibly get.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:05.789
"I am untethered and my rage knows no bounds!"

00:08:05.789 --> 00:08:10.349
While Howerton would have done a fine job
as Peter Quill, he arguably lacks the movie

00:08:10.349 --> 00:08:15.840
star gravitas with which Chris Pratt helped
send Guardians into the box office stratosphere.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.419
Had Howerton played Star-Lord, Guardians of
the Galaxy likely would have been widely regarded

00:08:20.419 --> 00:08:25.691
as a quirky, under-the-radar space romp destined
for cult classic status somewhere down the road.

00:08:25.691 --> 00:08:31.930
Instead, with Pratt in the lead role, it became
a surprise smash and one of the most successful

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:34.039
franchises in the Marvel pantheon.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:41.120
Before he was the King of Atlantis, Jason
Momoa was almost Drax the Destroyer.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:46.070
The actor had previously played barbaric brutes
such as Conan the Barbarian and Khal Drogo

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:50.830
in Game of Thrones, making him seem like the
perfect fit for a character like Drax.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:54.120
But this was the main reason why he didn't
take the part.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:59.100
Momoa didn't want to be typecast as a brutish
heavy-hitter, and especially didn't want his

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.160
kids to see him miserable in his work as a
result.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:06.120
That said, Momoa did enjoy auditioning with
Chris Pratt, later revealing:

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.660
"One of the funnest auditions I've ever done
in my life was with him."

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:16.340
Momoa is also cool that WWE-World-Champ-turned-Hollywood-heavyweight
Dave Bautista got the part.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:17.340
He said:

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.700
"I think it's perfectly cast.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.800
Dave is perfect for that role, for Drax."

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:27.540
Momoa would eventually get into the superhero
game himself, taking the lead in Aquaman and

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.450
becoming one of DC's most successful cinematic
heroes in the process.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.550
Two of Hollywood's biggest Hollywood comedy
heavyweights were also up for membership in

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.750
the Guardians of the Galaxy: Jim Carrey and
Adam Sandler.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:43.570
While still early in casting for the film,
Marvel checked on the availability of each

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:44.570
of them.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:49.060
It is uncertain, however, whether both actors
were up for the same part, or for different

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:50.060
roles.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:53.360
Understandably, there was speculation that
they were up for the roles of Rocket Raccoon

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.870
and/or Groot.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.480
As Marvel true believers know, those parts
eventually went to Bradley Cooper and Vin

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.980
Diesel respectively, though it is fun to consider
what Carrey and Sandler might have brought

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.320
to these characters.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:09.420
Would Carrey's Rocket Raccoon have had the
same mannerisms as Ace Ventura?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:13.990
Could Sandler's Groot have said "I am Groot"
in a voice similar to Bobby Boucher?

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:17.870
"One man said he wanted to decapitate me.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.900
Nobody else thought that to be too bad of
an idea."

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:22.980
All anyone can do is speculate.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.480
Still, it's fair to say things turned out
well in the end.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.481
Having first appeared in a mid-credits scene
of Captain America: The Winter Soldier, Scarlet

00:10:30.481 --> 00:10:35.860
Witch has gone on to become one of the MCU's
stalwart characters, even landing a full series

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.660
of her own in WandaVision.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:42.040
For the whole time, the character has been
performed by Elizabeth Olsen — but she wasn't

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.370
the only one up for the role.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:48.410
In fact, the part of Wanda Maximoff was reportedly
originally offered to Bronx-born, Dublin-raised

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.970
actor Saoirse Ronan.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:53.250
When Ronan allegedly passed on the part, it
went to Olsen.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:58.649
And given the massive success of WandaVision
on Disney+, the growing world and spinoffs

00:10:58.649 --> 00:11:03.680
that came out of that series, and her connection
to one Doctor Stephen Strange, it appears

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.709
that Olsen will continue cashing in her Marvel
checks for some time to come.

00:11:08.709 --> 00:11:12.570
Back in 2013, when Edgar Wright was still
attached to direct Ant-Man, there were two

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:18.200
actors in the running for the part of the
miniature marvel: Paul Rudd and Joseph Gordon-Levitt.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:22.380
Gordon-Levitt was just one year removed from
playing a version of Robin in Christopher

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:26.390
Nolan's final entry in The Dark Knight trilogy,
The Dark Knight Rises.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:30.550
At the time, Variety reported that he was
one of the final two actors being considered

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:35.990
for the part, alongside Rudd, who had a series
of leading roles in comedic hits under his

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:36.990
belt.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:41.010
That may have been what gave Rudd the nod
in the end, as Wright was apparently pushing

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:44.230
for an even more comedic tone than the other
Marvel movies.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:47.959
However, Gordon-Levitt later denied he was
ever in the running, saying the rumors were

00:11:47.959 --> 00:11:49.420
"nothing but lies."

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:53.790
Either way, it's all water under the bridge,
as Paul Rudd has returned for two sequels

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:57.380
to Ant-Man and a number of other MCU movies,
to boot.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:02.200
Of course, it wasn't just the title role that
was up for grabs when Edgar Wright was still

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.519
spearheading Ant-Man.

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:07.700
Two-time Academy Award-nominated actress Jessica
Chastain was rumored to have been offered

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.709
the role of the movie's "female lead."

00:12:09.709 --> 00:12:14.730
While sources originally speculated the role
was that of original Wasp Janet van Dyne,

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:19.149
it's now obvious that she likely would have
played Janet's daughter Hope, a part which

00:12:19.149 --> 00:12:20.950
ended up going to Evangeline Lilly.

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:26.279
Janet, of course, would eventually be played
by Michelle Pfeiffer in 2018's Ant-Man and

00:12:26.279 --> 00:12:27.279
the Wasp.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:31.779
An actor of Jessica Chastain's caliber certainly
would have given the lighthearted, action-packed,

00:12:31.779 --> 00:12:36.600
bug-centric romp some gravitas, much like
Hollywood legend Michael Douglas did in the

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.079
role of Dr. Hank Pym.

00:12:38.079 --> 00:12:41.260
Maybe we'll see her in the MCU somewhere down
the road.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:46.410
Academy Award-winning actor Joaquin Phoenix
was apparently not only in the running, but

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:51.750
the front runner to play the part of Marvel's
favorite sorcerer, Doctor Stephen Strange.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.750
Marvel wanted Phoenix for the role so much,
in fact, that he was rumored to be in final

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.180
negotiations before talks broke down.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:02.529
According to the acclaimed actor, it had nothing
to do with Marvel's more mainstream brand

00:13:02.529 --> 00:13:03.529
of entertainment.

00:13:03.529 --> 00:13:04.529
He later explained:

00:13:04.529 --> 00:13:07.709
"I think they make some great, fun movies.

00:13:07.709 --> 00:13:12.560
I enjoy those movies sometimes, and I think
they keep the f---ing industry going in some

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.100
ways, so I don't have a problem with it at
all...

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:18.250
I think everybody was really happy with how
things turned out.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:19.700
All parties were satisfied."

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:24.779
Basically, we have no idea what the issue
was, but in any event, Phoenix didn't take

00:13:24.779 --> 00:13:27.720
the part and it went to Benedict Cumberbatch
instead.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:32.949
Phoenix, true to his word that he has no problem
with comic book films, later played the genre's

00:13:32.949 --> 00:13:35.290
most infamous villain in Joker.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:41.410
In the late 1990s, pretty much every actor
who could convincingly play Spider-Man was

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.060
considered for the part.

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:50.050
Sometimes, "convincingly" wasn't even a consideration,
and some unusual choices outright lobbied

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:53.720
for the role, from Charlie Sheen to Michael
Jackson.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:58.950
Obviously, not all of these people were seriously
considered — in the 2000s, however, Tobey

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:03.690
Maguire put on the mask for three movies,
before being replaced by Andrew Garfield in

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.550
the Amazing Spider-Man films.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:11.180
Cut to 2015 and Spider-Man was being recast,
this time for the MCU.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:17.320
Again, everybody under the age of 22 was under
consideration, and among the final choices

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:20.110
were Asa Butterfield and Tom Holland.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.600
Spoiler Alert: Holland got it.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.800
Even so, Butterfield isn't disappointed, later
telling Collider:

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:30.470
"Every so often there's a part that you really
want [...] and you don't get it.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:35.500
And it is tough and it is s---, but I often
find that something even better comes out

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.509
of it at the end.

00:14:36.509 --> 00:14:40.339
And so in the case of Spider-Man, I did [Sex
Education]."

00:14:41.449 --> 00:14:47.630
It's hard to picture anyone but Samuel L.
Jackson as Nick Fury — but apparently, Jackson

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.560
wasn't the first actor approached.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:52.180
In fact, that honor goes to George Clooney.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:56.470
Honestly, you can actually kinda see this
working, especially if they were going for

00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:01.730
the gray templed, skirt-chasing, 1960s-style
super spy version of the character.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:06.269
And Clooney even considered taking the role,
at least enough to pick up a copy of Fury,

00:15:06.269 --> 00:15:08.649
the 2001 comic written by Garth Ennis.

00:15:08.649 --> 00:15:11.750
That, however, turned out to be a big mistake.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:16.279
Clooney was reportedly horrified by the absurdly
violent series.

00:15:16.279 --> 00:15:20.570
Apparently, the scene that particularly killed
Clooney's interest in the MCU involved Fury

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:22.790
strangling a man with his own intestines.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:27.570
Meanwhile, Mark Millar and Brian Hitch's The
Ultimates had already reimagined Nick Fury

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:33.399
as a certain iconic Hollywood star, and so,
in a case of life imitating art, Samuel L.

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:34.759
Jackson was given the part.

00:15:35.759 --> 00:15:41.310
Robert Downey Jr. and Gwyneth Paltrow go together
like salt and, well, Pepper.

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:45.910
However, the Academy Award-winning Paltrow
was not Iron Man director Jon Favreau's first

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.920
choice for the part of Pepper Potts.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.640
In fact, the director was so high on his main
choice that the Iron Man script was sent exclusively

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.370
to Favreau's favorite: Rachel McAdams.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:16:01.680
Back in the mid-2000s, McAdams was still basking
in the warm afterglow of Mean Girls and The

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:04.949
Notebook, and consequently had her pick of
parts.

00:16:04.949 --> 00:16:09.529
Evidently Iron Man's love interest wasn't
high on her list of priorities, though apparently

00:16:09.529 --> 00:16:11.690
The Time Traveler's Wife was.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.449
"I wouldn't change anything."

00:16:14.449 --> 00:16:18.630
While McAdams wasn't to play a part in Marvel's
inception, she later took the role of Stephen

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:23.399
Strange's love interest, Dr. Christine Palmer,
in Doctor Strange — and is due to return

00:16:23.399 --> 00:16:26.000
in Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:32.518
Perhaps Master of Mystic Arts is more her
type than billionaire military arms industrialist?

00:16:33.119 --> 00:16:38.980
Among the most prized of all female superhero
roles are characters such as Wonder Woman,

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.579
Catwoman, and Storm.

00:16:40.579 --> 00:16:45.079
But after the multi-billion dollar success
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, lesser-known

00:16:45.079 --> 00:16:48.560
characters suddenly came into play as potential
blockbuster heroines.

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:53.430
One of these was Carol Danvers, otherwise
known as Captain Marvel. 25 years ago, Danvers

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:58.250
was most famous to comic book fans as the
superhero who X-Men character Rogue put into

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.540
a coma when she stole her powers.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.940
Now, her popularity rivals that of Wonder
Woman.

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.800
That's quite the turnaround.

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:09.500
Before Oscar-winner Brie Larson snagged the
part, however, a few other big names wanted

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:10.790
to play Captain Marvel.

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:14.700
At a press junket for Jurassic World, Bryce
Dallas Howard revealed that she wanted to

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.560
play a part in a Marvel movie.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:20.810
When interviewer Eric Eisenberg suggested
Captain Marvel, Howard responded:

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:23.400
"Yes, let's start a campaign now.

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:24.700
That would be rad."

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:28.040
Another actress who shared her enthusiasm
was Olivia Wilde.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:32.270
When Meadowland director Reed Morano tweeted
to the film's star, Olivia Wilde, that they

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:35.340
should work on Captain Marvel together, Wilde
tweeted back:

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:36.880
"Oh hell yea.

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:37.930
Let's do this."

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:43.960
While we can't say either Howard or Wilde
were "almost" Captain Marvel, we can be reasonably

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:47.200
sure that they would have jumped at the opportunity.

